{
  "_how_to_add_a_tag": [
    "1. Scan the tag with any ISO 15693 reader (a phone with NFC Tools, a Flipper Zero, or this brick: it logs the numbers over USB).",
    "2. Copy the second byte of block 0 into `len`. That is the payload length, and it is the only identifier you need to get started.",
    "3. Optionally add `crc32` (the brick logs it). Two different tags can share a length; the CRC tells them apart.",
    "4. Pick a `profile` from sounds.json and a `colour`. No code changes are needed.",
    "`kind` is identity (a figure) or item (a tile). `combat: true` makes the tag fire on red and take hits from other bricks.",
    "Entries with `len: null` have not been scanned yet. The emulator uses `placeholder_len` so you can still try them, and labels them as placeholders. Do not flash a placeholder length to a real brick."
  ],
